# Platizio subagents (achilles + cybrilla-boss)

This project uses two dedicated subagents. Prefer them for feature and page work.

## When to use which

| Task | Agent |
|------|-------|
| New React page, backend endpoint, full E2E flow | **achilles** |
| Cybrilla/FP API facts, sandbox data, KYC/payment/mandate workflow | **cybrilla-boss** |
| Cybrilla-backed page (most distributor screens) | **both** — cybrilla-boss first for API contract, achilles implements |

## Invoke

```text
@.cursor/agents/achilles.md @.cursor/agents/cybrilla-boss.md build [PAGE]: [goal]
```

Or pick **Achilles** / **Cybrilla Boss** from the agent picker after reloading Cursor.

## Paths

- Backend: `platiziowealthtech-Back_end` — API `http://localhost:8081/api/v1`
- Frontend: `../platiziowealthtech-Front_End for now/platiziowealthtech-Front_End_sample`
- Investor actions: `http://localhost:8081/investor-actions/{token}` (not Vite :3000)

## Rules

- React → Platizio `/api/v1` only. Never call FP/POA from the browser.
- Orders use POA catalogue `mf_scheme_plans/cybrillapoa`, not OMS `fund_schemes`.
- Read `page-build-playbook.md` and `page-cybrilla-map.md` before building pages.
- Check `pending-work.md` for known gaps before claiming a flow is done.

